{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Distant explosion in a valley",
  "description": "Artillery landing far away on the other side of a mountain valley, heard from a hillside on a still evening. There is no crack: the air has taken all the highs. What arrives is a soft, wide 'whump' of low noise, felt as much as heard, with a second, weaker arrival just behind it by another path (the 'ka-rump' of far guns). Then the valley plays with it: an echo off the near slope, another off the far wall, each darker and softer, over a low ground roll that heaves and wanders and takes a long time to die.",
